  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Goalkeeper: block with the body",
  "description": "Two outfield players stand in front of the goal and lift loose balls towards the goalkeeper's upper body, taking turns. The goalkeeper keeps their arms behind their back and tries to stop the balls with the upper body.\n\nThe goalkeeper works on balance while moving and learns to get the body behind the ball. The balls should be lifted gently, not shot. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Lift the ball gently – this is not a shooting drill."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: move your whole body behind the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: stand stable with your weight on the balls of your feet."
    }
  ],
